OpenSSL / TLS follow-up
========================

- [ ] Bind OCI Bearer token realms to an allowed HTTPS origin, or require an
      explicit trusted-token-service configuration before sending registry
      credentials.
- [ ] Prevent production OCI configurations from selecting plaintext HTTP;
      restrict BPM_OCI_SCHEME=http to safe local/test endpoints and warn loudly.
- [ ] Make BPM_OCI_CA_FILE handling consistent: support the documented PEM
      format, including bundles, or reject DER and multi-certificate input
      during validation. Do not silently ignore X509_STORE_add_cert failures.
- [ ] Normalize certificates accepted by `bpm key add` to DER before placing
      them at the target cert.der path, or reject PEM input explicitly.
- [ ] NUL-terminate buffered HTTP responses before token parsing, or replace
      strstr/strchr parsing with length-bounded parsing.
- [x] Build the target TLS closure with static mbedTLS and an mbedTLS-backed
      static libcurl; retain OpenSSL for the operator and CMS signer.
- [x] Keep target/operator objects in separate profile directories so backend
      headers and ABI types cannot be mixed.
- [x] Require mbedTLS 3.6+ with PKCS#7 enabled and document the target
      SHIRUDO_TARGET_PKG_CONFIG_PATH dependency.
- [ ] Add target-side tests covering HTTPS verification, custom CA files,
      CA bundles, rejected HTTP/auth configurations, Bearer challenges, and
      PEM/DER certificate installation.
